\f0\fs24 \cf2 This is not 
\f1\i just
\f0\i0  a piano. It\'92s a small hidden masterpiece, a magical meeting of music, ingenuity, and love for the past. The Bagatti Valsecchi brothers were determined to have a piano in their home, partly to please Carolina Borromeo, who came from a family where music animated every celebration. But there was a problem: a piano in the Renaissance living room? It just couldn\'92t be seen! The solution? Brilliant. They designed a cabinet that concealed the piano inside, perfectly in the style of the 15th century. This way, the elegance of the home remained intact\'85 but with a simple opening, the strings of modernity would vibrate. The result is this magnificent instrument, crafted by Achille Merico, which is not only functional but breathtakingly beautiful. Look at the sides: those heart-shaped decorations? They\'92re not a romantic whim but an intellectual reference, inspired by a detail from the bench of the Palazzo del Comune in Pistoia, dating back to the 16th century. The brothers made a pencil sketch on graph paper
\fs16 \sub , 
\fs24 \nosupersub precise, meticulous, full of passion \'96 and transformed it into relief.\
A gesture that tells you everything about their spirit: love for art, attention to detail, a desire to unite the past and the present.\
And you? Had you figured out that inside that cabinet beat a musical heart?\
